# WK Core SRS migration (Anki replaces WK reviews)

This project is migrating **core WaniKani reviews** (radicals → kanji → vocab) to Anki + FSRS with in-Anki unlock logic. Work is spec-driven.

## Before any implementation or design change

1. **Read** [docs/wk_core_srs_design.md](../../docs/wk_core_srs_design.md) in full — especially:
   - **Agent resume checklist**
   - **Implementation status**
   - **Session log** (last entries)
   - **Open decisions**
2. After compaction, context reset, or new session on this feature: **start here**, not from memory.

## After any change to core SRS, scheduling bootstrap, or wk_unlock

Update [docs/wk_core_srs_design.md](../../docs/wk_core_srs_design.md):

- Bump **Last updated** date
- Tick **Implementation status** rows
- Append one line to **Session log**
- Resolve or add **Open decisions** if scope shifted

## Scope boundaries

- **In scope:** `--deck core`, `patch_apkg_wk_scheduling`, `WkSubjectId` / `PrerequisiteIds` fields, `anki_addon/wk_unlock`, supplementary suspend/gating, filtered deck search updates for `-is:suspended`
- **Out of scope for this rule:** grammar/cloze template tweaks unless adding link fields for gating; unrelated deck generators

## Template version reminder

Changing note-type **fields** or templates for core models requires bumping `MODEL_TEMPLATE_VERSIONS` per `.cursor/rules/wk-anki-template-versions.mdc`.

## Do not

- Re-introduce weekly Python runs to sync unlock state (belongs in `wk_unlock` addon)
- Re-apply WK scheduling on every re-import after `wk-schedule-bootstrapped` is set
- Use `--only-started` as the long-term gating mechanism for supplementary decks once addon ships
